  "version": 1,
  "description": "Sign-up display-name golden cases run by Android SignUpDisplayNameGoldenTest and iOS SignUpDisplayNameGoldenTests, and checked against a JS mirror of the server static rules by tests/display-name-contract.test.mjs. cases: input is the raw submitted name; normalized is the trimmed, whitespace-collapsed name the client sends as display_name (null = the client rejects it and sends nothing). reason of a rejected case is length (outside 2..32 Unicode code points after trim and collapse; the server accepts 2..40, the client keeps the stricter 32), characters (anything but letters, digits, space, dot, dash, underscore, or any control character) or server (the static public.safe_leaderboard_display_name rules: 7 or more ASCII digits, link or domain patterns such as www., discord.gg, t.me/ and name.com/.net/.org/.io/.gg, an @, or no letter or digit). Every accepted name must also pass the server rules, so the profile upsert trigger cannot reject it. The blocked-terms table is dynamic and is not covered. draftCases: what the live sign-up field keeps while typing (letters, digits, space, dot, dash, underscore; whitespace runs collapse to one space; clamp to 32 code points).",
